From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: describe Samsung Matisse LCD assembly

Add an opt-in diagnostic SM-T531 native MDP5/DSI/TC358764/LVDS graph.
The normal board DT retains the verified simpledrm recovery path.
Use Samsung r01 porch values confirmed by MDP and DSI register readback,
and a 60 Hz pixel clock rather than the bootloader 61.68 Hz PLL rate.

NOT PRODUCTION: bridge supplies remain firmware-powered, explicitly
selected by tc358764.firmware_power=1. Their wiring and LCD part identity
are unresolved; do not claim suspend or power-cycle validation.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/panel/panel-lvds.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/panel/panel-lvds.yaml
index b89f86bc0..9abedcce1 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/panel/panel-lvds.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/panel/panel-lvds.yaml
@@ -63,6 +63,8 @@ properties:
           # Riverdi RVT70HSLNWCA0 7.0" WSVGA (1024x600) TFT LCD LVDS panel
           - riverdi,rvt70hslnwca0
           # Samsung LTN070NL01 7.0" WSVGA (1024x600) TFT LCD LVDS panel
+          # Samsung SM-T531 LCD assembly; module identity unresolved
+          - samsung,matisse3g-lcd
           - samsung,ltn070nl01
           # Samsung LTN101AL03 10.1" WXGA (800x1280) TFT LCD LVDS panel
           - samsung,ltn101al03
